WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.850
In September of 1944,

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:11.310
due to the efforts of the 501st Joint Fighter Wing, "Strike Witches",

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.320
the Neuroi were expelled from Gallia.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.530
Subsequently, due to many fierce battles across Europe,

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.000
the front line had been pushed all the way to the border of Karlsland.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:28.630
All the while, Gallia walks the gradual path of reconstruction.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.630
Pas-de-Calais, Republic of Gallia

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.550
It looks like more people are returning to this area.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.680
Free Gallian Air Force

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.680
Flying Officer Perrine Clostermann

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.970
Let's see...

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.010
Commonwealth of Britannia Air Force

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.010
Flight Sergeant Lynette Bishop

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.600
Contributions to the armed forces have risen as well.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.310
Free Gallian Air Force

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.310
Sergeant Amelie Planchard

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.310
There's so much data.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.040
It's about time for our strikers to be overhauled, isn't it?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.450
If we're done with the report,
we should go to the base for maintenance.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:03.910
Oh, the base has moved?

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.280
Yes.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.580
The front line has just moved up to the Rhine.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.920
Then, where will our strikers be repaired?

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.090
In order to clear the area of Neuroi,

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:18.640
In order to clear the area of Neuroi,
we will be relocating our base to Arnhem.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:18.640
we will be relocating our base to Arnhem.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.760
Arnhem?

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.310
Is it safe to move it that close to the front line?

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.820
Not to worry.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.920
Not to worry, it will be located along the more secure southern bank.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.920
It will be located along the more secure south bank.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.290
Our offensive base is located along the northern bank.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.220
Alright, then, please take care of our strikers.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.070
Of course, we'll take great care.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.230
That day when I held up my hand

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.300
And saw a far-away light

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.290
Gertrud Barkhorn

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.290
Erica Hartmann

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.290
Minna-Dietlinde Wilcke

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.380
Piercing between my fingers

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.500
I swore to the sky

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.890
Charlotte E. Yeager

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.890
Francesca Lucchini

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.540
I'd cut through this storm

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.480
Faster than the speed of sound

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.600
Lynette Bishop

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.600
Perrine H. Closterman

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.730
On magic wings

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.970
To protect your smile

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.190
Sanya V. Litvyak

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.190
Eila Ilmatar Juutilainen

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:15.730
Painfully, I start to cry

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.560
But you come to my side again

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.420
I absolutely will not give up

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.450
This blue, blue place

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.850
Sakamoto Mio

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.740
"Come on, let's fly!"

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.840
If I could fly I'd shield you with

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.630
My overflowing courage

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.870
And I would shake off

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:41.140
The approaching dark

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:45.380
Stronger than yesterday

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.570
I will head into

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:55.310
That familiar, sparkling sky

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.170
Arnhem Bridge

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.670
Pas-de-Calais Harbor

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.000
These are today's goods.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.050
Thank you.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:24.270
We keep getting a little more everyday.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.780
Hey you!

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:29.770
Stop, thief!

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.360
Oh dear.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.950
Give it back! That's mine!

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:44.740
Medicine?

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.950
Lynette-san?

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.000
Huh?

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.230
Who are you?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.000
Hold on Rose,

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.260
Hold on Rose, I brought the medicine.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.260
I got the medicine.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.470
She has an incredible fever.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.150
Jean-Paul-san.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:06.970
Right away.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.220
Please, bring her on board.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.520
H-hey, are you really gonna help her?

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:17.150
Don't worry, she'll be alright.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.820
Of course, we will remain on standby until further notice.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.450
Understood.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.470
Good luck, Commander Minna.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.370
Perrine-san.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.180
What's happened?

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.420
Her fever...

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.590
We don't have a minute to spare.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:46.040
Jean-Paul, prepare the guest room and call a doctor.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.300
Right away.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.760
Amelie-san, boil some hot water.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.020
Okay.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.270
What is this place?

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.980
How is she, doctor?

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:08.070
It appears that she was about to develop
pneumonia from weakening due to malnutrition.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:13.930
With proper meals and rest, she should be fine in a few days.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.580
Thank goodness.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.850
Thank you, you've been a big help.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.010
No, I should be the thankful one here.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:26.420
After all, you're the one who provided the supplies and medicine.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.060
Hey, is she really important or something?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.920
Perine-san is the lady of this area, making her the most important person around here.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.660
The most?!

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.440
Wow!

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:43.190
I'll take my leave.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.700
I don't have any money.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:50.400
It's okay, we'll look after her until she is fully recovered.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.530
No kiddin', four-eyes?

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.620
What a bad mouth.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.420
This is awful, what is it?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.710
Chamomile tea, it's good for your body.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.600
Where are your parents?

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.680
Where are you from?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.630
We don't have any parents anymore.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:16.020
We snuck away after the evacuation.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.210
Oh my...

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.980
Where did you live beforehand?

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.440
My home, Holt Street in Arnhem.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:30.260
Holt Street, on the north side of the river?
They're clearing the Neuroi out of there right now.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.450
I know I'm not allowed to go back,
but there's something important I have to get.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.960
I made a promise to Rose.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:47.150
The clean up of Arnhem should take two weeks,
once it's over I can take you there.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.470
Until then, you're free to stay here.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.930
Really, no lie?

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:53.780
What a distrustful child.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.350
We can contact the base from here,
so we'll know when they're all done.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.110
Then, it's a promise!

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:04.570
A flea?

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.530
Stop it! What're you doin'?

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.160
Just be cooperative!

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:26.340
Fleas aren't just a parasite, they're a pest who must be taken out before they begin to double.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:28.510
Why you—

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.390
Are you trying to kill me? You stupid four-eyes.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.420
Get back here!

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.770
Stop running!

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.900
They're getting along well.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.030
I guess...

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:52.500
I've won.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.370
Dammit.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.260
You're all white now.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.930
Let's go take a bath.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:08.050
Rose's fever might go down if she has a nice-looking brother to help her.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.660
Her fever's started to go down.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.680
Thank goodness.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.210
Did you have a nice rest?

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.450
You're alright, this is my home.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.120
Your brother is here too.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:32.040
Ann isn't here...

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:32.650
Ann?

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.160
Achoo!

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:36.660
Here.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.660
Use this. You can have it.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:46.080
You're a really nice lady, y'know?

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.340
Perrine-san is nice too.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.210
No way four-eyes is.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.680
Rose?

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.750
What's wrong?

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.440
Are you hurt anywhere?

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.330
Are you okay, Rose?

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:17.230
Look, Ann is right here.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.310
Ann!

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.940
It's okay, Big Bro is here.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:25.710
Yeah!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.600
Goodness.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.250
So she was just afraid she had lost her bear.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.700
It's not some bear, it's Ann.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:33.880
Yes, of course.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:37.640
Was it good?

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.640
Yeah. Thank you for helping me.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:43.620
You're welcome.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:45.750
Your sister is a good child.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:49.770
Big Bro, when are you gonna save Yan?

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.230
Yan?

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:54.490
Yan is Ann's big brother!

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.240
When we had to leave our home, I left him behind.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:02.080
Since I have my big brother here, I'm not sad.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.080
But since Ann is all alone, I think she's sad.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:11.570
So that important thing you left behind was Yan.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.230
You were just thinking of your sister.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:17.210
That's none of your business.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.030
How unacceptable.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.660
Use your knife and fork properly.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.400
Shaddup.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.000
Who cares how I eat?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:55.420
How is it?

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:58.920
It's good, isn't it Ann?

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.020
Wait right there!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.410
That's my bread!

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.660
Shove it!

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.870
What is this?

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.420
Do you like books?

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.560
N-not really, I can't read.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.010
I could teach you.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.220
Really?

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:33.070
Oh, studying. How admirable.

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.730
Isn't it?

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.500
Something must've caught his interest to learn.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:43.240
The repairs on the west wall are coming along quickly, aren't they?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.370
They are, thanks to everyone's great work.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.870
Stupid four-eyes

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:53.720
This must be that child's work.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:02.510
Goodness. I thought he could be a nice boy at heart, but he really is just trouble.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:02.510
Goodness. How could such a nice girl be related to such a rude boy.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.720
Remember, he's just a child.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:10.000
That's true. I just want the evactuation to be done with already.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:14.410
Once the evacuation is over,
where will he really be able to go?

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:18.440
Britannia is already filled with refugees,
they're even starting to turn them away.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.190
Just 10 more days to go.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:24.330
We still can't go home?

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:28.450
Just a little longer. We have to wait until you're all better after all.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:29.900
Yeah.

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:33.040
And don't worry, we'll get your brother back soon.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.210
Isn't that great, Ann?

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.690
Thank you for your help.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.130
I'm just returning the favor.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:48.910
Who's that?

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.210
It looks like the 506th.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:53.100
You bastards!

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.350
You lying witches!

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.240
Julius?

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:58.100
What's wrong?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.660
If they had just came like they said...

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.980
Dad would've...

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:09.360
Hurry up and get them out of here! The Neuroi are coming!

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.360
4 Years Ago

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.360
Arnhem, Netherlands

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.990
We cannot let the Neuroi through here until we finish with the children's evacuation!

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.500
Dad, I'm scared.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:19.000
Julius, right now the witches are on their way.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.500
The witches are gonna come?

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.010
Yeah, and they'll send the Neuroi running.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:28.260
After that, I'll come for you.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:32.090
Come right away!

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:45.530
Dad!

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:50.920
Where are the witches?

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:56.950
You said they would come!

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.000
Oh my...

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:04.500
Julius thinks the witches abandoned him.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:10.090
The defenders at Arnhem were overwhelmed, by the time we arrived we couldn't help them at all.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.760
But they weren't abandoned.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:18.020
But if that's what Julius thinks happened, I don't think there's any way we can change his mind.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:23.020
We shouldn't say anything about being witches.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.650
Big Bro...

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:37.950
What's all this?

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.560
Julius?

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.330
Why's there so much food?

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.790
I bet that stupid four-eyes is hogging it all for herself!

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.600
Perrine-san isn't that type of person.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:50.090
We give all of these to the surrounding villages.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:51.840
You give them?

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:56.400
Perrine-san puts all of her money towards things like this.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.400
Things like relief and aid for people affected by the war.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.050
She has?

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.110
But, what is she doing to make money in the first place?

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:09.070
Well, she does a lot of stuff.

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:10.930
Stuff?

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:21.410
Watch out!

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.510
You're...

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:40.350
a witch.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.440
This is... um...

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.650
What just happened?

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.460
Amelie-san.

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.610
I'm sorry.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:53.200
You're...

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.840
You're all witches, aren't you!

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:11.460
Is this everything?

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:15.340
Yes, please take it to the Arnhem base.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.840
Arnhem?

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.370
Alright.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.860
Without that troublemaker around it's nice and quiet, isn't it?

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:42.350
He doesn't want to eat with us because we're witches.

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:45.580
In any case, he'll come and eat when he gets hungry.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.860
Julius isn't here!

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:50.460
Where did Big Bro go?

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:51.590
Huh?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.550
He's gone?

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.090
We looked everywhere for him.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.840
You don't think he hid on the military truck from earlier?

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:59.520
It was headed for Arnhem!

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:01.840
That would mean, he's going back to his house!

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.560
Hurry, we have to contact the base.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.400
I can't contact them with the phone.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:09.810
The radio's not working either.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:12.920
You don't think this could be because of the Neuroi?

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:16.950
We have no other choice but to head out and see firsthand.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.600
I wanna go too!

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:22.620
Don't worry, we'll bring your brother back.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.490
Be a good girl and wait here, alright?

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:29.420
Amelie-san, head to the St. Trond base and inform Commander Minna of the situation.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.180
Roger.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:32.380
Lynne-san, you and I will prepare to sortie.

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:37.130
But our weapons and strikers are all being held at the Arnhem base.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:39.890
You're right...

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:41.890
Milady.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:50.510
One must always be prepared in one's moment of need.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:53.020
I hope these are sufficient.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.150
Splendid job, Jean-Paul.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:01.170
Joint Forces Western Frontline Base, Arnhem

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.390
That's the Arnhem base.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:34.360
He's not here.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.360
Maybe we were wrong.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:37.940
Look!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.950
I gave this to him.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:41.200
He was definitely here.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.120
Lynne-san, go and retrieve your striker from the base.

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.830
What about you?

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.250
I'm going to look for the boy.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.590
There aren't any Neuroi here.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.340
I knew those witches were liars.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.060
Thank God, it's still standing.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.120
There he is!

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.240
Yan, I found you!

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.000
Sorry I left you all alone.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.230
This too.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:00.030
Alright.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.280
N-Neuroi.

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:25.080
Get up, Julius.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.220
Where'd all that energy go, you troublemaker.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.220
Four-eyes...

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:50.030
If we can cross the bridge we'll be back in controlled land.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:50.740
Hurry!

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:13.520
A-awesome!

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:15.270
Hold on tight.

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:22.240
Hurry, we're almost there!

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:23.020
Please be quiet.

00:22:32.610 --> 00:22:33.490
It's huge!

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:00.190
Ouch.

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:03.020
Four-eyes, you're bleeding!

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:06.280
Don't worry.

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:11.420
There. I'll get the Neuroi's attention.

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:14.030
That's when you'll need to run.

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:18.080
But, your leg is injured, isn't it?

00:23:18.820 --> 00:23:20.080
Aren't you scared?

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.210
Even if you're a witch, that's a monster!

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:33.090
Come on, let's go.

00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:04.860
Four-eyes!

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:08.510
What're you doin'? Hurry and get up!

00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:11.600
Oh goodness...

00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:14.010
But, it's all okay now.

00:24:22.870 --> 00:24:23.650
See?

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:28.400
It's running!

00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:32.700
It went into the water tower!

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:34.160
This could be troublesome.

00:24:38.290 --> 00:24:39.670
I can't hit it in there.

00:24:48.390 --> 00:24:49.460
Julius!

00:24:49.780 --> 00:24:52.470
You said that was a <i>water</i> tower?

00:24:52.470 --> 00:24:54.720
Y-yeah.

00:25:02.230 --> 00:25:03.270
My leg...

00:25:04.900 --> 00:25:05.890
Wait, Julius!

00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:07.230
Come back!

00:25:11.380 --> 00:25:12.330
Julius!

00:25:21.130 --> 00:25:22.700
Julius...

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:29.590
Looking for this?

00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:33.970
Don't scare me like that.

00:25:39.230 --> 00:25:42.310
Lynne-san, aim for that!

00:25:42.310 --> 00:25:43.390
Roger!

00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:57.410
Tonnerre!

00:26:04.410 --> 00:26:05.410
Now!

00:26:18.090 --> 00:26:20.350
W-we did it!

00:26:20.660 --> 00:26:22.930
What do you think?  This is a witches—

00:26:24.110 --> 00:26:25.710
Your hair's all messed up!

00:26:26.670 --> 00:26:28.810
You damned brat!

00:26:29.530 --> 00:26:32.110
Hey, that hurts! Stop it!

00:26:32.110 --> 00:26:34.460
I will not stop!

00:26:38.700 --> 00:26:40.950
That was a real disaster.

00:26:41.530 --> 00:26:44.750
There were still that many ground Neuroi there?

00:26:44.750 --> 00:26:46.640
Rose, look!

00:26:47.560 --> 00:26:48.370
Yan!

00:26:48.370 --> 00:26:50.370
Thank you Big Bro!

00:26:50.370 --> 00:26:51.800
That's great, isn't it Ann?

00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:55.680
Ann, your brother is back!

00:26:55.680 --> 00:26:57.380
You don't have to be lonely anymore!

00:26:58.900 --> 00:27:00.300
That's very nice,

00:27:00.300 --> 00:27:03.350
but didn't you get anything else?

00:27:04.660 --> 00:27:05.970
A book.

00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:07.730
My dad gave it to me.

00:27:08.730 --> 00:27:10.730
He wanted me to read it to Rose.

00:27:11.090 --> 00:27:13.780
Can you read it?

00:27:14.980 --> 00:27:15.980
I can't.

00:27:17.810 --> 00:27:20.670
Then, I will have to teach you how to read, properly.

00:27:21.130 --> 00:27:23.740
I guess that's fine, if you want to teach me.

00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:27.080
Well, then school is in session.

00:27:27.620 --> 00:27:28.680
School?

00:27:28.680 --> 00:27:29.250
Yes.

00:27:29.250 --> 00:27:33.840
And, starting today, you will be able to call this place home.

00:27:36.110 --> 00:27:41.610
No matter what I will never let go of this hand

00:27:41.610 --> 00:27:49.920
If you can embrace hope then let's fly into the future

00:27:57.880 --> 00:28:02.340
I keep searching for my old dreams

00:28:03.070 --> 00:28:07.320
When the things that matter are right here inside of me

00:28:07.410 --> 00:28:12.420
I will not give up the feelings that you gave to me

00:28:12.550 --> 00:28:15.610
Or forget them as I move forward

00:28:17.770 --> 00:28:23.890
Because after the tears and the kind words

00:28:24.020 --> 00:28:29.840
I will become stronger and begin to soar

00:28:30.300 --> 00:28:35.630
No matter what I will never let go of this hand

00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:40.680
It's alright if we reach for our desires together

00:28:40.710 --> 00:28:46.070
No matter what I will never let this light go out

00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:54.300
With the sky reflected in my eyes let's fly into tomorrow

00:29:06.470 --> 00:29:08.140
2 Weeks Later

00:29:06.830 --> 00:29:09.760
Alright everybody, did you get all of that?

00:29:09.760 --> 00:29:12.090
Yes, Ms. Perrine.

00:29:13.130 --> 00:29:15.270
Perrine-san! Urgent news!

00:29:15.270 --> 00:29:17.690
Yoshika-chan is on her way here!

00:29:18.520 --> 00:29:20.020
Miyafyji-san is?

00:29:20.920 --> 00:29:25.780
<i>Lynne-chan, Perrine-san how have you been? I'm doing well.</i>

00:29:25.780 --> 00:29:30.790
<i>It's a little unexpected, but I'm going to study abroad at a Helvetian medical school.</i>

00:29:30.790 --> 00:29:36.790
<i>When I arrive in Pas-de-Calais in one month, I'd be really happy to see you again!</i>

00:29:36.790 --> 00:29:38.480
In one month?

00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:40.280
Um... Today is...

00:29:40.870 --> 00:29:43.200
That's only 3 weeks!

00:29:43.200 --> 00:29:46.800
I've got to find her some kind of gift.

00:29:46.800 --> 00:29:48.550
What would be good?

00:29:48.550 --> 00:29:50.810
If it's a medical school, why not a white robe?

00:29:51.980 --> 00:29:53.390
That's a great idea!

00:29:53.500 --> 00:29:55.640
Petersburg, Empire of Orussia
502nd Joint Fighter Wing Frontline Base

00:29:54.830 --> 00:29:55.640
Jeez.

00:29:55.640 --> 00:29:57.650
What's wrong, Eila?

00:29:58.130 --> 00:30:01.360
It looks like Perrine just went
through something greatly troubling.

00:30:01.360 --> 00:30:03.570
How do you know?

00:30:01.390 --> 00:30:03.570
Suomus Air Force
Flight Sergeant Nikka Edvardine Katajainen

00:30:03.930 --> 00:30:07.450
Huh? You're still doubting my fortune-telling?

00:30:04.150 --> 00:30:07.160
Suomus Air Force
Flying Officer Eila Ilmatar Juutilainen

00:30:07.450 --> 00:30:10.160
Empire of Orussia Army

00:30:07.450 --> 00:30:10.160
Flying Officer Sanya V. Litvyak

00:30:07.810 --> 00:30:10.410
Well, once in awhile it's the complete opposite of what you say.

00:30:10.950 --> 00:30:12.460
Is that true?

00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:14.080
Empire of Orussia Army

00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:14.080
Flight Lieutenant Aleksandra I. Pokryshkin

00:30:12.460 --> 00:30:17.120
It is! That's the reason I got struck by lightning and crashed the other day.

00:30:17.120 --> 00:30:19.580
That's not my fault, you know!

00:30:19.580 --> 00:30:20.810
Then who's fault is it?

00:30:20.810 --> 00:30:22.290
It's just because you're unlucky!

00:30:22.300 --> 00:30:24.300
Like that could be the reason.

00:30:29.050 --> 00:30:31.100
<i>So, the operation is going well?</i>

00:30:31.100 --> 00:30:34.030
We're managing, somehow or another.

00:30:34.030 --> 00:30:36.350
<i>That's good to hear. Will you be coming our way?</i>

00:30:36.350 --> 00:30:39.020
No, not yet.

00:30:36.800 --> 00:30:40.810
Empire of Fuso Navy
Squadron Leader Sakamoto Mio

00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:41.380
We've still got a lot left to do here.

00:30:41.380 --> 00:30:42.110
<i>Right.</i>

00:30:42.650 --> 00:30:44.600
Did you hear Miyafuji is studying abroad?

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:47.880
<i>Yes, I got in touch with her the other day, before she left for Europe.</i>

00:30:47.880 --> 00:30:50.800
I see, that's good to hear.

00:30:51.820 --> 00:30:54.830
To Be Continued
